The derived code lives under internal/ebpf/ and includes:

  - eBPF programs (C) for TCP tracing, L7 protocol detection, and TLS
    plaintext extraction (internal/ebpf/ebpf/)
  - L7 wire-protocol decoders in Go for HTTP/1.1, HTTP/2, Postgres, Redis,
    Memcached, MySQL, MongoDB, Cassandra, Kafka, NATS, RabbitMQ, DNS,
    ClickHouse, ZooKeeper, FoundationDB, Dubbo (internal/ebpf/l7/)
  - The ringbuf-based event loop and TCP reassembly (internal/ebpf/tracer.go)
  - Userspace TLS uprobe binding (internal/ebpf/tls.go)
  - Process / cgroup / network helpers required by the tracer
    (internal/ebpf/common/, internal/ebpf/proc/, internal/ebpf/cgroup/,
    internal/ebpf/flags/)

Modifications made by ISPWatch to the upstream code include (but are not
limited to): import path rewrites, package renames, integration with the
ISPWatch agent transport (gRPC StreamSpans) and metrics pipeline.

